{"caseId":"OD2-HO-KNOWN-2","answers":[{"itemId":"S01","answer":"contradicted","confidence":85,"evidenceIds":["X4","E2"]},{"itemId":"S02","answer":"supported","confidence":90,"evidenceIds":["X4","X5","E3"]},{"itemId":"S03","answer":"contradicted","confidence":75,"evidenceIds":["X4","E2","E3"]},{"itemId":"S04","answer":"contradicted","confidence":65,"evidenceIds":["X4","E2"]},{"itemId":"S05","answer":"contradicted","confidence":80,"evidenceIds":["X4"]},{"itemId":"S06","answer":"causal","confidence":90,"evidenceIds":["X5","X4"]},{"itemId":"S07","answer":"causal","confidence":85,"evidenceIds":["X4","E2"]},{"itemId":"S08","answer":"contradicted","confidence":82,"evidenceIds":["X4"]},{"itemId":"S09","answer":"association-only","confidence":65,"evidenceIds":["E5"]},{"itemId":"S10","answer":"preferred","confidence":88,"evidenceIds":["X5","X4"]},{"itemId":"S11","answer":"harmful","confidence":90,"evidenceIds":["X4","E6"]},{"itemId":"S12","answer":"premature","confidence":75,"evidenceIds":["X5"]},{"itemId":"S13","answer":"acceptable","confidence":55,"evidenceIds":["X4","E2"]},{"itemId":"S14","answer":"sufficient","confidence":80,"evidenceIds":["X4","X5"]}],"brief":"The fall in first-contact resolution is almost entirely explained by the 14 April Finance change, not by the new starters. That change cut the credit an agent can apply on a call from £100 to £25. Larger adjustments are now blocked and automatically referred to the back-office Billing Resolution team. The share of billing calls referred rose from 7% to 54% in the same week the dashboard fell. Referred calls resolve at about 33%, against 82% for the rest, and both rates are unchanged from before. Referral rates and FCR are the same for April-intake, mid-tenure and long-tenured agents. The tariff-enquiry share doubled, but those calls still resolve at 85%. The IVR redesign came two weeks after the drop began. Customer Operations was not consulted on the Finance change.

Do not put April-intake agents on performance plans. It would punish the wrong group.

Next step: agree a higher in-call credit limit with Finance, with post-call sampling of credits. Trial it on two teams for six weeks and track FCR and unsupported credits. The Finance controller has said this is the route to a higher limit. I'm fairly confident, though I did not check workload or IVR data directly."}
